<title>ESTONIA: NORMA SHAREHOLDERS APPROVE PROFIT DISTRIBUTION.</title>
<headline>NORMA SHAREHOLDERS APPROVE PROFIT DISTRIBUTION.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The shareholders of Estonian industrial concern Norma on Friday approved a board proposal for the distribution of the company's 1996 profit.</p>
<p>The shareholders agreed to pay dividends of 10 percent on the nominal value of the company's shares or one kroon per share.</p>
<p>The dividends will reach 13.2 million kroons out of the 1996 net profit of 63.3 million kroons.</p>
<p>They also approved a board proposal to retain the rest of the profit or 50.1 million kroons.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
